    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **55 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the create-owner endpoint while keeping the flat `address` input working. Changes:\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields` (so they appear on both the request DTO and the response `Owner`).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so a structured-only payload is no longer rejected by bean validation. The `address` field's description now documents it as the composed, normalized read value.\n\n**Validation** (`ValidateOwnerFields.java`)\n- An owner is now valid when it supplies an address in *either* form: a non-blank normalized `addressLine1` or a non-blank normalized flat `address`. City/firstName/lastName/telephone requirements are unchanged, so earlier minimal owners are still accepted.\n\n**Normalization + composition** (`NormalizeOwnerAddress.java`)\n- When `addressLine1` is present, both lines are normalized (upper-case, whitespace collapse, `ST\u2192STREET` etc.) and the entity's `address` is set to the composed string \u2014 normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when `addressLine2` is present. Otherwise the flat `address` is normalized on its own. Because everything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality) reads the already-composed `address`/`postcode`/`city`, it transparently uses the structured fields when present and falls back to the flat address.\n\n**Persistence** (`Owner.java` + `db/*/schema.sql`, `db/hsqldb/data.sql`)\n- Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields and `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns so the structured lines round-trip through GET (MapStruct maps them by name). For hsqldb (the test DB, which uses positional `INSERT`s) I placed the new columns at the end of the table and appended two trailing NULLs to the seed inserts.\n\nThe four spec tests (Cp01 either-form/missing-city rejection, Cp12/Cp44 normalization + composition + flat-address backward compat, Cp30 locality from structured postcode) and all 51 other tests are green.",
